# Vercel hosts the frontend, API and Better Auth server. Postgres is the Neon
# Marketplace resource managed through Vercel, not an external Neon Auth service.
# DATABASE_URL is injected by that integration and is server-only. Runtime
# connections use the pooled endpoint with TLS certificate verification.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://…pooled-neon-runtime-url…
# DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=postgresql://…direct-neon-migration-url…
#
# Server-only: generate an independent secret from 48 cryptographically random
# bytes for each environment. The server requires at least 32 characters.
# Use Sensitive for Preview/Production; Vercel Development uses encrypted Config
# so its separate local-development value can be pulled. Never commit a value
# or use a VITE_ prefix.
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
#
# Optional explicit application origin, without a path/query/fragment. Vercel
# deployment/branch metadata supplies preview origins automatically. Set the
# final HTTPS production origin only after it is chosen. Outside Vercel, local
# development can use a matching loopback origin and its own secret/database.
# BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# Production must explicitly select its own Neon project and canonical HTTPS
# origin. Do not copy the Preview connection or the pilot account into it.
# SAJDA_PRODUCTION_NEON_PROJECT=
# SAJDA_CANONICAL_ORIGIN=https://your-verified-domain
# SAJDA_SEO_INDEXING=noindex
# A production build requires configured email and matching database/auth origins.
# Passing that configuration check is not proof of payment or email delivery.
#
# Required for real verification, password-reset and contact email. Configure a Resend
# API key plus a sender mailbox on an actually verified domain. Both are server
# configuration; never expose credentials through browser-prefixed variables.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# SAJDA_EMAIL_FROM=
# Contact forms always deliver to dev@hypbit.com, with the visitor as Reply-To.
# Account emails go ONLY to the account owner, with dev@hypbit.com as Reply-To;
# no recovery or verification link is copied to the operator mailbox.
# Use an existing verified Resend sender if available. A recipient mailbox alone
# does not verify a sending domain. Do not replace inbound MX records to enable
# outgoing mail. Keep open/click tracking off for password-reset links.
#
# Without valid email configuration, signup, reset requests and verification
# resend return 503. Public domain search remains usable. API success does not
# prove inbox delivery: verify a received email before approving account launch.
# Vercel builds derive VITE_ACCOUNT_AUTH_ENABLED from server configuration.
# Legacy VITE_NEON_AUTH_URL is blanked by that build; NEON_AUTH_BASE_URL and
# NEON_AUTH_COOKIE_SECRET are not used. Do not configure managed Neon Auth.
# Never create VITE_DATABASE_URL, VITE_BETTER_AUTH_SECRET or VITE_RESEND_API_KEY.
VITE_PUBLIC_SEARCH_MODE=false

NAME_QUEST_WEB_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1
NAME_QUEST_WEB_PORT=8080
# AI is optional and server-only. Creative search and Deep Review keep their
# deterministic local fallback when the gateway is disabled or unavailable.
# No provider is selected implicitly: configure each enabled feature with an
# explicit Vercel AI Gateway model ID in provider/model format. Only the
# reviewed low-cost models google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite and
# google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite are accepted; no automatic model fallback.
AI_GATEWAY_ENABLED=false
# AI_GATEWAY_BRIEF_MODEL=provider/model
# AI_GATEWAY_REVIEW_MODEL=provider/model
# AI_GATEWAY_NAMING_MODEL=google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite
# Naming generates labels; no model can supply availability or price evidence.
#
# Shared server-enforced AI request allowance: 50 per UTC day by default,
# configurable up to a hard maximum of 100. Naming and review notes consume
# the same allowance. Per IP: 3 per UTC day; global concurrency: 2.
# Completed requests may follow immediately. Failed attempts still consume quota.
# Missing quota storage fails closed to the deterministic fallback.
# SAJDA_AI_DAILY_LIMIT=50
#
# Vercel deployments authenticate through the deployment's OIDC identity.
# For local or non-Vercel execution only, an optional AI Gateway key may be
# configured server-side. Never create VITE_AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY or send it to
# the browser. No direct provider credentials are required by these features.
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=
#
# The gateway helper always requires disallowPromptTraining=true and
# zeroDataRetention=true (per-request ZDR requires Vercel Pro/Enterprise).
# No compliant provider means local fallback, never weaker privacy routing.
# There is no optional switch that permits prompt training. Never include sensitive data
# in a search brief. AI may interpret a brief or add short editorial notes,
# but cannot change deterministic review scores/order or verify availability,
# price, trademarks, ownership, or legal status.

# Provider comparison is deliberately safe by default. The public release
# fetches a verified price only from Loopia's published price list. Other
# providers are shown as official checkout links until a provider-specific,
# reviewed adapter is implemented. Do not add browser-facing VITE_ secrets.
# The server recognises NAME_QUEST_PROVIDER_<ID>_PRICE_API_URL and _TOKEN as
# connector placeholders, but setting them alone never enables scraping or a
# live price. Keep tokens server-only in Vercel Project Environment Variables.
# Supported future adapter IDs: cloudflare, godaddy, namecheap, porkbun,
# dynadot, route53, onecom, ionos, ovhcloud, squarespace, hostinger, gandi,
# hover, spaceship, namecom, namesilo, alibabacloud, internetbs, wix.

# Optional server-side standard-TLD price comparison feed. Add this only to
# the Vercel Project Environment Variables (or the server process environment)
# when the TLDES integration is enabled. Never use VITE_TLDES_API_KEY: that
# would expose the secret in the browser bundle. The feed returns published
# standard registration/renewal pricing for a TLD, cached for up to one hour;
# it is not a quote for an exact domain, premium name, promotion, tax amount,
# or checkout total.
# TLDES_API_KEY=

# Self-service developer API keys require Neon migration 0013. The control
# plane mints scoped, expiring, environment-bound 256-bit
# `sj_live_…`/`sj_test_…` tokens, store only SHA-256 digests in Neon, and return
# each raw token exactly once. Never add a raw API key or database credential to
# a VITE_ variable.
#
# Optional legacy fallback for integrations provisioned before self-service
# keys. Store only comma- or newline-separated SHA-256 hashes as
# `client_id:64_lowercase_hex_hash`; this list cannot be managed in the UI.
# SAJDA_API_KEY_HASHES=
# Legacy operator keys are search-only; they cannot read private accounts or MCP.
# MCP /api/mcp and REST /api/v1/account use the same scoped account keys.
#
# Native iPhone authorization requires migration 0014 and explicit enablement.
# Keep disabled in production until that environment is verified independently.
# No native credential or Vercel protection bypass belongs in the app bundle.
SAJDA_NATIVE_ENABLED=false
# Build-only, public configuration for npm run build:native:
# SAJDA_NATIVE_API_ORIGIN=https://your-verified-sajda-backend

# Optional evidence-first market context. The only accepted value today is
# `namebio-tldstats`, which enables a fixed, free aggregate TLDStats request
# with attribution. It never enables NameBio individual-sale endpoints or
# accepts a source URL. Keep production disabled until a reviewed shared cache
# and scheduled ingestion job enforce the source's global rate limit.
# SAJDA_FACT_SIGNAL_SOURCES=namebio-tldstats

# Trading research: server-only, all disabled unless explicitly enabled after
# migrations 0009/0010/0011/0012 and a reviewed source-catalog/worker verification.
# A 24-source/600-name ceiling does NOT enable or license new crawl sources.
# SAJDA_LOST_DOMAINS_ENABLED=false
# SAJDA_LOST_DOMAINS_CRON_ENABLED=false
# SAJDA_LOST_DOMAINS_ARCHIVE_ENABLED=false
# Optional exact-domain, read-only Porkbun availability/price observations.
# Credentials remain server-only. Sandbox/mock responses are not live evidence.
# No registration, renewal, transfer or purchase actions are performed.
# Enabled Trading accounts can explicitly refresh an existing report candidate's
# exact quote without restarting technical research. The server reserves each
# attempt: max 60/account/24 hours, one pending/account, 60s/domain cooldown.
# Retries reuse a request UUID; previous technical/price dates are not renewed.
# A production build rejects enabled pricing with absent/invalid/sandbox keys.
# SAJDA_LOST_DOMAINS_REGISTRAR_ENABLED=false
# PORKBUN_API_KEY=
# PORKBUN_SECRET_API_KEY=
# CRON_SECRET=replace-with-a-unique-server-secret-at-least-32-characters
# Enable recurring work only after verifying the Vercel plan, reviewed sources,
# runtime and database. Add the /api/cron/lost-domains schedule to vercel.json
# explicitly (every 1-5 minutes); keep the function maxDuration at 60 seconds.
# The production build fails when cron is enabled without that configuration.
# A schedule entry alone is not evidence that unattended work actually runs.
